<section background-color="heading">
  <grid spacing="none">
    <grid-item colspan="35" vertical-align="center">
      <p role="eyebrow">History detective case · Southern Brazil · 1835–1845</p>
      <h1 font-size="44pt">What can three objects tell us?</h1>
      <p font-size="lg"><b>A tax paper. A folded map. A letter from home.</b></p>
      <p>Each holds a clue about the Ragamuffin War, known in Portuguese as the <i>Revolução Farroupilha</i>.</p>
      <spacer mode="fixed" size="18pt"/>
      <labels><label variant="solid">Our mystery</label></labels>
      <p font-size="lg">Why did it last from 1835 to 1845—and how did it affect different lives?</p>
    </grid-item>
    <grid-item colspan="25" padding="0">
      <ai-image background="true" image-style="southern-brazil-paper-museum" aspect-ratio="portrait" prompt="Layered cut-paper museum-table illustration of three carefully arranged objects from nineteenth-century southern Brazil: a blank tax paper with wax seal, a folded schematic map with no lettering, and a tied letter from home, colored-pencil shading on warm cream paper, postcard red question marks as small paper cutouts, river blue and sun yellow accents, clear daylight, no people, no weapons, no legible text"/>
    </grid-item>
  </grid>
</section>